In a recent exchange, James responded to John Ure's extensive email discussing the concept of an International Green Bank (IGB) aimed at enhancing climate finance, particularly for the Global South. John introduced himself as a political economist and shared insights from his publications, emphasizing the IGB's potential role in displacing multilateral development banks (MDBs) while fostering more engaged governance. James acknowledged John's paper and expressed interest in the proposal, highlighting the importance of a distinct decision-making structure and the political feasibility of the IGB. He raised questions about the perception of MDBs towards the IGB and the distribution of decision-making power among governments. While recognizing the challenges, James encouraged John to further promote his idea in relevant forums and invited him for a Zoom chat to explore the topic further.
